From: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@arm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:43:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: properly ignore depth-stencil aspectMask

From the Vulkan spec:

> The aspectMask of any image view specified for pDepthAttachment or
> pStencilAttachment is ignored. Instead, depth attachments are
> automatically treated as if VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_DEPTH_BIT was specified
> for their aspect masks, and stencil attachments are automatically
> treated as if VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_STENCIL_BIT was specified for their
> aspect masks.

We implement this in get_z_pan_image_view and get_s_pan_image_view, but
we ended up using the original, aspect-restricted views instead. Move
the calls earlier so we can do this properly instead.

This fixes the following (recently added) dEQP tests for me:
- dEQP-VK.renderpasses.*.depth_stencil_resolve.samples_*.d32_sfloat_s8_uint.*_testing_stencil_ignore_depth_aspect

Fixes: deb8b5c9c78e ("panvk: Avoid direct MSAA resolves to AFBC on v6 and earlier")
Reviewed-by: Yiwei Zhang <zzyiwei@chromium.org>
(cherry picked from commit 25e1e2397727e2534ee2950f298a2a7993f06e69)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit 3f936d37395)

Backported to the 26.2.4-based fork: the src/ hunks applied as is; .pick_status.json (not in the fork's
history as such) was left out.

